# Files Shopify CLI must never upload (theme push, theme dev, and the
# Lighthouse CI action, which pushes a development theme from the repo root).
#
# Syntax (Shopify CLI 5): one pattern per line, matched against the theme
# file key (for example assets/base.css). Glob patterns match the basename
# when they have no slash. Patterns wrapped in /.../ are regular expressions.
# A bare directory such as "docs/" never matches; use a regex or "dir/*".
#
# CLI 5 only collects theme folders (assets, blocks, config, layout, locales,
# sections, snippets, templates) plus root AGENTS.md and DESIGN.md, so the
# non-theme folders below are listed as a guard against future CLI changes
# and against copies placed inside a theme folder by mistake.
#
# config/settings_data.json is deliberately NOT ignored: the Shopify GitHub
# integration owns it. To avoid overwriting live customizer settings on a
# local push, use: shopify theme push --unpublished --ignore config/settings_data.json

# Non-theme content. Never upload to Shopify.
/^(docs|headless-poc|scripts|\.github|\.shopify)\//
*.zip
*.backup
*.md
.theme-check.yml
.gitattributes
.gitignore
.shopifyignore
